      "requiresAttunement": false,
      "rulesText": "Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Uncommon (+1), Rare (+2), or Very Rare (+3)\n\nYou have a bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. The bonus is determined by the weapon's rarity."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/magic-items/weapon-of-warning",
      "@type": "MagicItem",
      "name": "Weapon of Warning",
      "slug": "weapon-of-warning",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Magic Items",
        "section": "10.292",
        "heading": "Weapon of Warning",
        "lineStart": 17745,
        "lineEnd": 17753
      },
      "itemCategory": "Weapon",
      "categoryDetail": "Any Simple or Martial",
      "rarity": "Uncommon",
      "requiresAttunement": true,
      "attunementNote": "Requires Attunement",
      "rulesText": "Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Uncommon (Requires Attunement)\n\nAs long as this weapon is within your reach and you are attuned to it, you and allies within 30 feet of you gain the following benefits.\n\nAlarm. The weapon magically awakens each subject who is sleeping naturally when combat begins. This benefit doesn't wake a subject from magically induced sleep.\n\nSupernatural Readiness. Each subject has Advantage on its Initiative rolls."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/magic-items/well-of-many-worlds",
      "@type": "MagicItem",
      "name": "Well of Many Worlds",
      "slug": "well-of-many-worlds",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Magic Items",
        "section": "10.293",
        "heading": "Well of Many Worlds",
        "lineStart": 17755,
        "lineEnd": 17763
      },
      "itemCategory": "Wondrous Item",
      "rarity": "Legendary",
      "requiresAttunement": false,
      "rulesText": "Wondrous Item, Legendary\n\nThis fine black cloth, soft as silk, is folded up to the dimensions of a handkerchief. It unfolds into a circular sheet 6 feet in diameter.\n\nYou can take a Magic action to unfold the Well of Many Worlds and place it on a solid surface, whereupon it forms a two-way, 6-foot-diameter, circular portal to another world or plane of existence. Each time the item opens a portal, the GM decides where it leads. The portal remains open until a creature within 5 feet of it takes a Magic action to close it by taking hold of the edges of the cloth and folding it up.\n\nOnce the Well of Many Worlds has opened a portal, it can't do so again for 1d8 hours."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/magic-items/wind-fan",
      "@type": "MagicItem",
      "name": "Wind Fan",
      "slug": "wind-fan",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Magic Items",
        "section": "10.294",
        "heading": "Wind Fan",
        "lineStart": 17765,
        "lineEnd": 17769
      },
      "itemCategory": "Wondrous Item",
      "rarity": "Uncommon",
      "requiresAttunement": false,
      "rulesText": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon\n\nWhile holding this fan, you can cast Gust of Wind (save DC 13) from it. Each subsequent time the fan is used before the next dawn, it has a cumulative 20 percent chance of not working; if the fan fails to work, it tears into useless, nonmagical tatters."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/magic-items/winged-boots",
      "@type": "MagicItem",
      "name": "Winged Boots",
      "slug": "winged-boots",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Magic Items",
        "section": "10.295",
        "heading": "Winged Boots",
        "lineStart": 17771,
        "lineEnd": 17775
      },
      "itemCategory": "Wondrous Item",
      "rarity": "Uncommon",
      "requiresAttunement": true,
      "attunementNote": "Requires Attunement",
      "rulesText": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)\n\nThese boots have 4 charges and regain 1d4 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing the boots, you can take a Magic action to expend 1 charge, gaining a Fly Speed of 30 feet for 1 hour. If you are flying when the duration expires, you descend at a rate of 30 feet per round until you land."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/magic-items/wings-of-flying",
      "@type": "MagicItem",
      "name": "Wings of Flying",
      "slug": "wings-of-flying",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Magic Items",
        "section": "10.296",
        "heading": "Wings of Flying",
        "lineStart": 17777,
        "lineEnd": 17783
      },
      "itemCategory": "Wondrous Item",
      "rarity": "Rare",
      "requiresAttunement": true,
      "attunementNote": "Requires Attunement",
      "rulesText": "Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)\n\nWhile wearing this cloak, you can take a Magic action to turn the cloak into a pair of wings on your back. The wings lasts for 1 hour or until you end the effect early as a Magic action. The wings give you a Fly Speed of 60 feet. If you are aloft when the wings disappear, you fall. When the wings disappear, you can't use them again for 1d12 hours.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/monsters/aboleth",
      "@type": "Monster",
      "name": "Aboleth",
      "slug": "aboleth",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Monsters A-Z",
        "section": "12.2",
        "heading": "Aboleth",
        "lineStart": 18068,
        "lineEnd": 18123
      },
      "sizeTypeAlignment": "Large Aberration, Lawful Evil",
      "sizeAndType": "Large Aberration",
      "alignment": "Lawful Evil",
      "armorClass": "17",
      "initiative": "+7 (17)",
      "hitPoints": "150 (20d10 + 40)",
      "speed": "10 ft., Swim 40 ft.",
      "skills": "History +12, Perception +10",
      "senses": "Darkvision 120 ft.; Passive Perception 20",
      "languages": "Deep Speech; telepathy 120 ft.",
      "challenge": "10 (XP 5,900, or 7,200 in lair; PB +4)",
      "armorClassValue": 17,
      "hitPointsValue": 150,
      "hitPointsRoll": {
        "expression": "20d10+40",
        "count": 20,
        "sides": 10,
        "modifier": 40
      },
      "challengeRating": "10",
      "experiencePoints": 5900,
      "proficiencyBonus": 4,
      "abilities": {
        "str": {
          "score": 21,
          "modifier": 5,
          "savingThrow": 5
        },
        "dex": {
          "score": 9,
          "modifier": -1,
          "savingThrow": 3
        },
        "con": {
          "score": 15,
          "modifier": 2,
          "savingThrow": 6
        },
        "int": {
          "score": 18,
          "modifier": 4,
          "savingThrow": 8
        },
        "wis": {
          "score": 15,
          "modifier": 2,
          "savingThrow": 6
        },
        "cha": {
          "score": 18,
          "modifier": 4,
          "savingThrow": 4
        }
      },
      "statSections": [
        {
          "name": "Traits",
          "rulesText": "Amphibious. The aboleth can breathe air and water.\n\nEldritch Restoration. If destroyed, the aboleth gains a new body in 5d10 days, reviving with all its Hit Points in the Far Realm or another location chosen by the GM.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Lair). If the aboleth fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMucus Cloud. While underwater, the aboleth is surrounded by mucus. Constitution Saving Throw: DC 14, each creature in a 5-foot Emanation originating from the aboleth at the end of the aboleth's turn. Failure: The target is cursed. Until the curse ends, the target's skin becomes slimy, the target can breathe air and water, and it can't regain Hit Points unless it is underwater.\n\nWhile the cursed creature is outside a body of water, the creature takes 6 (1d12) Acid damage at the end of every 10 minutes unless moisture is applied to its skin before those minutes have passed.\n\nProbing Telepathy. If a creature the aboleth can see communicates telepathically with the aboleth, the aboleth learns the creature's greatest desires.",
          "sourceLocator": {
            "chapter": "Monsters A-Z",
            "section": "12.2",
            "heading": "Traits",
            "lineStart": 18089,
            "lineEnd": 18101
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Actions",
          "rulesText": "Multiattack. The aboleth makes two Tentacle attacks and uses either Consume Memories or Dominate Mind if available.\n\nTentacle. Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 15 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 5) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the Grappled condition (escape DC 14) from one of four tentacles.\n\nConsume Memories. Intelligence Saving Throw: DC 16, one creature within 30 feet that is Charmed or Grappled by the aboleth. Failure: 10 (3d6) Psychic damage.\n\nSuccess: Half damage. Failure or Success: The aboleth gains the target's memories if the target is a Humanoid and is reduced to 0 Hit Points by this action.\n\nDominate Mind (2/Day). Wisdom Saving Throw: DC 16, one creature the aboleth can see within 30 feet. Failure: The target has the Charmed condition until the aboleth dies or is on a different plane of existence from the target. While Charmed, the target acts as an ally to the aboleth and is under its control while within 60 feet of it. In addition, the aboleth and the target can communicate telepathically with each other over any distance.\n\nThe target repeats the save whenever it takes damage as well as after every 24 hours it spends at least 1 mile away from the aboleth, ending the effect on itself on a success.",
          "sourceLocator": {
            "chapter": "Monsters A-Z",
            "section": "12.2",
            "heading": "Actions",
            "lineStart": 18103,
            "lineEnd": 18115
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Legendary Actions",
          "rulesText": "Legendary Action Uses: 3 (4 in Lair). Immediately after another creature's turn, the aboleth can expend a use to take one of the following actions. The aboleth regains all expended uses at the start of each of its turns.\n\nLash. The aboleth makes one Tentacle attack.\n\nPsychic Drain. If the aboleth has at least one creature Charmed or Grappled, it uses Consume Memories and regains 5 (1d10) Hit Points.",
          "sourceLocator": {
            "chapter": "Monsters A-Z",
            "section": "12.2",
            "heading": "Legendary Actions",
            "lineStart": 18117,
            "lineEnd": 18123
          }
        }
      ],
      "rulesText": "Large Aberration, Lawful Evil\n\nAC 17\nInitiative +7 (17)\nHP 150 (20d10 + 40)\nSpeed 10 ft., Swim 40 ft.\n\nSkills History +12, Perception +10\nSenses Darkvision 120 ft.; Passive Perception 20\nLanguages Deep Speech; telepathy 120 ft.\nCR 10 (XP 5,900, or 7,200 in lair; PB +4)\n\nTraits\n\nAmphibious. The aboleth can breathe air and water.\n\nEldritch Restoration. If destroyed, the aboleth gains a new body in 5d10 days, reviving with all its Hit Points in the Far Realm or another location chosen by the GM.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Lair). If the aboleth fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMucus Cloud. While underwater, the aboleth is surrounded by mucus. Constitution Saving Throw: DC 14, each creature in a 5-foot Emanation originating from the aboleth at the end of the aboleth's turn. Failure: The target is cursed. Until the curse ends, the target's skin becomes slimy, the target can breathe air and water, and it can't regain Hit Points unless it is underwater.\n\nWhile the cursed creature is outside a body of water, the creature takes 6 (1d12) Acid damage at the end of every 10 minutes unless moisture is applied to its skin before those minutes have passed.\n\nProbing Telepathy. If a creature the aboleth can see communicates telepathically with the aboleth, the aboleth learns the creature's greatest desires.\n\nActions\n\nMultiattack. The aboleth makes two Tentacle attacks and uses either Consume Memories or Dominate Mind if available.\n\nTentacle. Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 15 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 5) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the Grappled condition (escape DC 14) from one of four tentacles.\n\nConsume Memories. Intelligence Saving Throw: DC 16, one creature within 30 feet that is Charmed or Grappled by the aboleth. Failure: 10 (3d6) Psychic damage.\n\nSuccess: Half damage. Failure or Success: The aboleth gains the target's memories if the target is a Humanoid and is reduced to 0 Hit Points by this action.\n\nDominate Mind (2/Day). Wisdom Saving Throw: DC 16, one creature the aboleth can see within 30 feet. Failure: The target has the Charmed condition until the aboleth dies or is on a different plane of existence from the target. While Charmed, the target acts as an ally to the aboleth and is under its control while within 60 feet of it. In addition, the aboleth and the target can communicate telepathically with each other over any distance.\n\nThe target repeats the save whenever it takes damage as well as after every 24 hours it spends at least 1 mile away from the aboleth, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nLegendary Actions\n\nLegendary Action Uses: 3 (4 in Lair). Immediately after another creature's turn, the aboleth can expend a use to take one of the following actions. The aboleth regains all expended uses at the start of each of its turns.\n\nLash. The aboleth makes one Tentacle attack.\n\nPsychic Drain. If the aboleth has at least one creature Charmed or Grappled, it uses Consume Memories and regains 5 (1d10) Hit Points.",
      "attacks": [
        {
          "name": "Tentacle",
          "attackType": "Melee",
          "damageComponents": [
            {
              "averageDamage": 12,
              "damageType": "Bludgeoning",
              "damageRoll": {
                "expression": "2d6+5",
                "count": 2,
                "sides": 6,
                "modifier": 5
              }
            }
          ],
          "sourceText": "Tentacle. Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 15 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 5) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the Grappled condition (escape DC 14) from one of four tentacles.",
          "path": "statSections[1].rulesText.paragraphs[1]",
          "parseStatus": "parsed",
          "attackBonus": 9,
          "reachFeet": 15
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/monsters/adult-black-dragon",
