        "section": "5.12",
        "heading": "Fighting Style Feats",
        "lineStart": 5833,
        "lineEnd": 5833
      },
      "section": "5.12"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/rules/5-17-epic-boon-feats",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Epic Boon Feats",
      "slug": "5-17-epic-boon-feats",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Feats",
        "section": "5.17",
        "heading": "Epic Boon Feats",
        "lineStart": 5859,
        "lineEnd": 5859
      },
      "section": "5.17"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/rules/5-2-feat-descriptions",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Feat Descriptions",
      "slug": "5-2-feat-descriptions",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Feats",
        "section": "5.2",
        "heading": "Feat Descriptions",
        "lineStart": 5753,
        "lineEnd": 5755
      },
      "section": "5.2",
      "rulesText": "The feats that follow are organized by category - Origin, General, Fighting Style, or Epic Boon - and alphabetized in each category."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/rules/5-3-parts-of-a-feat",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Parts of a Feat",
      "slug": "5-3-parts-of-a-feat",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Feats",
        "section": "5.3",
        "heading": "Parts of a Feat",
        "lineStart": 5757,
        "lineEnd": 5767
      },
      "section": "5.3",
      "rulesText": "The description of a feat contains the following parts, which are presented after the feat's name.\n\nCategory. A feat is a member of a category, which is noted in the feat. If you're instructed to choose a feat from a specific category, such as the Origin category, that category must appear under the feat's name. If you're instructed to choose a feat and no category is specified, you can choose from any category.\n\nPrerequisite. To take a feat, you must meet any prerequisite in its description unless a feature allows you to take the feat without the prerequisite. If a prerequisite includes a class, you must have at least 1 level in that class to take the feat.\n\nBenefit. The benefits of a feat are detailed after any prerequisites are listed. If you have a feat, you gain its benefits.\n\nRepeatable. A feat can be taken only once unless its description states otherwise in a “Repeatable” subsection."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/rules/5-4-origin-feats",
      "@type": "Rule",
      "name": "Origin Feats",
      "slug": "5-4-origin-feats",
      "source": {
