    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/spells/fear",
      "@type": "Spell",
      "name": "Fear",
      "slug": "fear",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Spells",
        "section": "7.146",
        "heading": "Fear",
        "lineStart": 9176,
        "lineEnd": 9187
      },
      "level": 3,
      "school": "Illusion",
      "classAvailability": [
        "Bard",
        "Sorcerer",
        "Warlock",
        "Wizard"
      ],
      "castingTime": "Action",
      "range": "Self",
      "components": "V, S, M (a white feather)",
      "duration": "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
      "rulesText": "Level 3 Illusion (Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)\n\nCasting Time: Action\nRange: Self\nComponents: V, S, M (a white feather)\nDuration: Concentration, up to 1 minute\n\nEach creature in a 30-foot Cone must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or drop whatever it is holding and have the Frightened condition for the duration.\n\nA Frightened creature takes the Dash action and moves away from you by the safest route on each of its turns unless there is nowhere to move. If the creature ends its turn in a space where it doesn't have line of sight to you, the creature makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a successful save, the spell ends on that creature.",
      "classes": [
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/bard"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/sorcerer"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/warlock"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/wizard"
        }
      ],
      "savingThrowAbility": "Wisdom",
      "scalesWithSlotLevel": false,
      "concentration": true,
      "ritual": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/spells/feather-fall",
      "@type": "Spell",
      "name": "Feather Fall",
      "slug": "feather-fall",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Spells",
        "section": "7.147",
        "heading": "Feather Fall",
        "lineStart": 9189,
        "lineEnd": 9198
      },
      "level": 1,
      "school": "Transmutation",
      "classAvailability": [
        "Bard",
        "Sorcerer",
        "Wizard"
      ],
      "castingTime": "Reaction, which you take when you or a creature you can see within 60 feet of you falls",
      "range": "60 feet",
      "components": "V, M (a small feather or piece of down)",
      "duration": "1 minute",
      "rulesText": "Level 1 Transmutation (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard)\n\nCasting Time: Reaction, which you take when you or a creature you can see within 60 feet of you falls\nRange: 60 feet\nComponents: V, M (a small feather or piece of down)\nDuration: 1 minute\n\nChoose up to five falling creatures within range. A falling creature's rate of descent slows to 60 feet per round until the spell ends. If a creature lands before the spell ends, the creature takes no damage from the fall, and the spell ends for that creature.",
      "classes": [
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/bard"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/sorcerer"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/wizard"
        }
      ],
      "scalesWithSlotLevel": false,
      "concentration": false,
      "ritual": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/spells/find-familiar",
      "@type": "Spell",
      "name": "Find Familiar",
      "slug": "find-familiar",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Spells",
        "section": "7.148",
        "heading": "Find Familiar",
        "lineStart": 9200,
        "lineEnd": 9221
      },
      "level": 1,
      "school": "Conjuration",
      "classAvailability": [
        "Wizard"
      ],
      "castingTime": "1 hour or Ritual",
      "range": "10 feet",
      "components": "V, S, M (burning incense worth 10+ GP, which the spell consumes)",
      "duration": "Instantaneous",
      "rulesText": "Level 1 Conjuration (Wizard)\n\nCasting Time: 1 hour or Ritual\nRange: 10 feet\nComponents: V, S, M (burning incense worth 10+ GP, which the spell consumes)\nDuration: Instantaneous\n\nYou gain the service of a familiar, a spirit that takes an animal form you choose: Bat, Cat, Frog, Hawk, Lizard, Octopus, Owl, Rat, Raven, Spider, Weasel, or another Beast that has a Challenge Rating of 0. Appearing in an unoccupied space within range, the familiar has the statistics of the chosen form (see “Monsters”), though it is a Celestial, Fey, or Fiend (your choice) instead of a Beast. Your familiar acts independently of you, but it obeys your commands.\n\nTelepathic Connection. While your familiar is within 100 feet of you, you can communicate with it telepathically. Additionally, as a Bonus Action, you can see through the familiar's eyes and hear what it hears until the start of your next turn, gaining the benefits of any special senses it has.\n\nFinally, when you cast a spell with a range of touch, your familiar can deliver the touch. Your familiar must be within 100 feet of you, and it must\n\ntake a Reaction to deliver the touch when you cast the spell.\n\nCombat. The familiar is an ally to you and your allies. It rolls its own Initiative and acts on its own turn. A familiar can't attack, but it can take other actions as normal.\n\nDisappearance of the Familiar. When the familiar drops to 0 Hit Points, it disappears. It reappears after you cast this spell again. As a Magic action, you can temporarily dismiss the familiar to a pocket dimension. Alternatively, you can dismiss it forever. As a Magic action while it is temporarily dismissed, you can cause it to reappear in an unoccupied space within 30 feet of you. Whenever the familiar drops to 0 Hit Points or disappears into the pocket dimension, it leaves behind in its space anything it was wearing or carrying.\n\nOne Familiar Only. You can't have more than one familiar at a time. If you cast this spell while you have a familiar, you instead cause it to adopt a new eligible form.",
      "classes": [
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/wizard"
        }
      ],
      "scalesWithSlotLevel": false,
      "concentration": false,
      "ritual": true
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/spells/find-steed",
      "@type": "Spell",
      "name": "Find Steed",
      "slug": "find-steed",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Spells",
        "section": "7.149",
        "heading": "Find Steed",
        "lineStart": 9223,
        "lineEnd": 9240
      },
      "level": 2,
      "school": "Conjuration",
      "classAvailability": [
        "Paladin"
      ],
      "castingTime": "Action",
      "range": "30 feet",
      "components": "V, S",
      "duration": "Instantaneous",
      "rulesText": "Level 2 Conjuration (Paladin)\n\nCasting Time: Action\nRange: 30 feet\nComponents: V, S\nDuration: Instantaneous\n\nYou summon an otherworldly being that appears as a loyal steed in an unoccupied space of your choice within range. This creature uses the Otherworldly Steed stat block. If you already have a steed from this spell, the steed is replaced by the new one.\n\nThe steed resembles a Large, rideable animal of your choice, such as a horse, a camel, a dire wolf, or an elk. Whenever you cast the spell, choose the steed's creature type - Celestial, Fey, or Fiend - which determines certain traits in the stat block.\n\nCombat. The steed is an ally to you and your allies. In combat, it shares your Initiative count, and it functions as a controlled mount while you ride it (as defined in the rules on mounted combat). If you have the Incapacitated condition, the steed takes its turn immediately after yours and acts independently, focusing on protecting you.\n\nDisappearance of the Steed. The steed disappears if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you die. When it disappears, it leaves behind anything it was wearing or carrying. If you cast this spell again, you decide whether you summon the steed that disappeared or a different one.\n\nUsing a Higher-Level Spell Slot. Use the spell slot's level for the spell's level in the stat block.",
      "classes": [
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/paladin"
        }
      ],
      "scalesWithSlotLevel": true,
      "concentration": false,
      "ritual": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/spells/find-the-path",
      "@type": "Spell",
      "name": "Find the Path",
      "slug": "find-the-path",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Spells",
        "section": "7.151",
        "heading": "Find the Path",
        "lineStart": 9280,
        "lineEnd": 9293
      },
      "level": 6,
      "school": "Divination",
      "classAvailability": [
        "Bard",
        "Cleric",
        "Druid"
      ],
      "castingTime": "1 minute",
      "range": "Self",
      "components": "V, S, M (a set of divination tools - such as cards or runes - worth 100+ GP)",
      "duration": "Concentration, up to 1 day",
      "rulesText": "Level 6 Divination (Bard, Cleric, Druid)\n\nCasting Time: 1 minute\nRange: Self\nComponents: V, S, M (a set of divination tools - such as cards or runes - worth 100+ GP)\nDuration: Concentration, up to 1 day\n\nYou magically sense the most direct physical route to a location you name. You must be familiar with the location, and the spell fails if you name a destination on another plane of existence, a moving destination (such as a mobile fortress), or an unspecific destination (such as “a green dragon’s lair”).\n\nFor the duration, as long as you are on the same plane of existence as the destination, you know how far it is and in what direction it lies. Whenever you\n\nface a choice of paths along the way there, you know which path is the most direct.",
      "classes": [
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/bard"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/cleric"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/druid"
        }
      ],
      "scalesWithSlotLevel": false,
      "concentration": true,
      "ritual": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/spells/find-traps",
      "@type": "Spell",
      "name": "Find Traps",
      "slug": "find-traps",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Spells",
        "section": "7.152",
        "heading": "Find Traps",
        "lineStart": 9295,
        "lineEnd": 9306
      },
      "level": 2,
      "school": "Divination",
      "classAvailability": [
        "Cleric",
        "Druid",
        "Ranger"
      ],
      "castingTime": "Action",
      "range": "120 feet",
      "components": "V, S",
      "duration": "Instantaneous",
      "rulesText": "Level 2 Divination (Cleric, Druid, Ranger)\n\nCasting Time: Action\nRange: 120 feet\nComponents: V, S\nDuration: Instantaneous\n\nYou sense any trap within range that is within line of sight. A trap, for the purpose of this spell, includes any object or mechanism that was created to cause damage or other danger. Thus, the spell would sense the Alarm or Glyph of Warding spell or a mechanical pit trap, but it wouldn't reveal a natural weakness in the floor, an unstable ceiling, or a hidden sinkhole.\n\nThis spell reveals that a trap is present but not its location. You do learn the general nature of the danger posed by a trap you sense.",
      "classes": [
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/cleric"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/druid"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/ranger"
        }
      ],
      "scalesWithSlotLevel": false,
      "concentration": false,
      "ritual": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/spells/finger-of-death",
      "@type": "Spell",
      "name": "Finger of Death",
      "slug": "finger-of-death",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Spells",
        "section": "7.153",
        "heading": "Finger of Death",
        "lineStart": 9308,
        "lineEnd": 9319
      },
      "level": 7,
      "school": "Necromancy",
      "classAvailability": [
        "Sorcerer",
        "Warlock",
        "Wizard"
      ],
      "castingTime": "Action",
      "range": "60 feet",
      "components": "V, S",
      "duration": "Instantaneous",
      "rulesText": "Level 7 Necromancy (Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)\n\nCasting Time: Action\nRange: 60 feet\nComponents: V, S\nDuration: Instantaneous\n\nYou unleash negative energy toward a creature you can see within range. The target makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 7d8 + 30 Necrotic damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nA Humanoid killed by this spell rises at the start of your next turn as a Zombie (see “Monsters”) that follows your verbal orders.",
      "classes": [
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/sorcerer"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/warlock"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/wizard"
        }
      ],
      "savingThrowAbility": "Constitution",
      "damage": [
        {
          "damageType": "Necrotic",
          "damageRoll": {
            "expression": "7d8+30",
            "count": 7,
            "sides": 8,
            "modifier": 30
          }
        }
      ],
      "scalesWithSlotLevel": false,
      "concentration": false,
      "ritual": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/spells/fire-bolt",
      "@type": "Spell",
      "name": "Fire Bolt",
      "slug": "fire-bolt",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Spells",
        "section": "7.155",
        "heading": "Fire Bolt",
        "lineStart": 9336,
        "lineEnd": 9347
      },
      "level": 0,
      "school": "Evocation",
      "classAvailability": [
        "Sorcerer",
        "Wizard"
      ],
      "castingTime": "Action",
      "range": "120 feet",
      "components": "V, S",
      "duration": "Instantaneous",
      "rulesText": "Evocation Cantrip (Sorcerer, Wizard)\n\nCasting Time: Action\nRange: 120 feet\nComponents: V, S\nDuration: Instantaneous\n\nYou hurl a mote of fire at a creature or an object within range. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 1d10 Fire damage. A flammable object hit by this spell starts burning if it isn't being worn or carried.\n\nCantrip Upgrade. The damage increases by 1d10 when you reach levels 5 (2d10), 11 (3d10), and 17 (4d10).",
      "classes": [
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/sorcerer"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/wizard"
        }
      ],
      "damage": [
        {
          "damageType": "Fire",
          "damageRoll": {
            "expression": "1d10",
            "count": 1,
            "sides": 10
          }
        }
      ],
      "scalesWithSlotLevel": false,
      "concentration": false,
      "ritual": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/spells/fire-shield",
      "@type": "Spell",
      "name": "Fire Shield",
      "slug": "fire-shield",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Spells",
        "section": "7.156",
        "heading": "Fire Shield",
        "lineStart": 9349,
        "lineEnd": 9362
      },
      "level": 4,
      "school": "Evocation",
      "classAvailability": [
        "Druid",
        "Sorcerer",
        "Wizard"
      ],
      "castingTime": "Action",
      "range": "Self",
      "components": "V, S, M (a bit of phosphorus or a firefly)",
      "duration": "10 minutes",
      "rulesText": "Level 4 Evocation (Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard)\n\nCasting Time: Action\nRange: Self\nComponents: V, S, M (a bit of phosphorus or a firefly)\nDuration: 10 minutes\n\nWispy flames wreathe your body for the duration, shedding Bright Light in a 10-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 10 feet.\n\nThe flames provide you with a warm shield or a chill shield, as you choose. The warm shield grants you Resistance to Cold damage, and the chill shield grants you Resistance to Fire damage.\n\nIn addition, whenever a creature within 5 feet of you hits you with a melee attack roll, the shield erupts with flame. The attacker takes 2d8 Fire damage from a warm shield or 2d8 Cold damage from a chill shield.",
      "classes": [
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/druid"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/sorcerer"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/wizard"
        }
      ],
      "damage": [
        {
          "damageType": "Fire",
          "damageRoll": {
            "expression": "2d8",
            "count": 2,
            "sides": 8
          }
        },
        {
          "damageType": "Cold",
          "damageRoll": {
            "expression": "2d8",
            "count": 2,
            "sides": 8
          }
        }
      ],
      "scalesWithSlotLevel": false,
      "concentration": false,
      "ritual": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/spells/fire-storm",
      "@type": "Spell",
      "name": "Fire Storm",
      "slug": "fire-storm",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Spells",
        "section": "7.157",
        "heading": "Fire Storm",
        "lineStart": 9364,
        "lineEnd": 9375
      },
      "level": 7,
      "school": "Evocation",
      "classAvailability": [
        "Cleric",
        "Druid",
        "Sorcerer"
      ],
      "castingTime": "Action",
      "range": "150 feet",
      "components": "V, S",
      "duration": "Instantaneous",
      "rulesText": "Level 7 Evocation (Cleric, Druid, Sorcerer)\n\nCasting Time: Action\nRange: 150 feet\nComponents: V, S\nDuration: Instantaneous\n\nA storm of fire appears within range. The area of the storm consists of up to ten 10-foot Cubes, which you arrange as you like. Each Cube must be contiguous with at least one other Cube. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 7d10 Fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nFlammable objects in the area that aren't being worn or carried start burning.",
      "classes": [
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/cleric"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/druid"
