    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/spells/heat-metal",
      "@type": "Spell",
      "name": "Heat Metal",
      "slug": "heat-metal",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Spells",
        "section": "7.194",
        "heading": "Heat Metal",
        "lineStart": 9970,
        "lineEnd": 9983
      },
      "level": 2,
      "school": "Transmutation",
      "classAvailability": [
        "Bard",
        "Druid"
      ],
      "castingTime": "Action",
      "range": "60 feet",
      "components": "V, S, M (a piece of iron and a flame)",
      "duration": "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
      "rulesText": "Level 2 Transmutation (Bard, Druid)\n\nCasting Time: Action\nRange: 60 feet\nComponents: V, S, M (a piece of iron and a flame)\nDuration: Concentration, up to 1 minute\n\nChoose a manufactured metal object, such as a metal weapon or a suit of Heavy or Medium metal armor, that you can see within range. You cause the object to glow red-hot. Any creature in physical contact with the object takes 2d8 Fire damage when you cast the spell. Until the spell ends, you can take a Bonus Action on each of your later turns to deal this damage again if the object is within range.\n\nIf a creature is holding or wearing the object and takes the damage from it, the creature must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or drop the object if it can. If it doesn't drop the object, it has Disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks until the start of your next turn.\n\nUsing a Higher-Level Spell Slot. The damage increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 2.",
      "classes": [
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/bard"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/druid"
        }
      ],
      "savingThrowAbility": "Constitution",
      "damage": [
        {
          "damageType": "Fire",
          "damageRoll": {
            "expression": "2d8",
            "count": 2,
            "sides": 8
          }
        }
      ],
      "scalesWithSlotLevel": true,
      "concentration": true,
      "ritual": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/spells/hellish-rebuke",
      "@type": "Spell",
      "name": "Hellish Rebuke",
      "slug": "hellish-rebuke",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Spells",
        "section": "7.195",
        "heading": "Hellish Rebuke",
        "lineStart": 9985,
        "lineEnd": 9996
      },
      "level": 1,
      "school": "Evocation",
      "classAvailability": [
        "Warlock"
      ],
      "castingTime": "Reaction, which you take in response to taking damage from a creature that you can see within 60 feet of yourself",
      "range": "60 feet",
      "components": "V, S",
      "duration": "Instantaneous",
      "rulesText": "Level 1 Evocation (Warlock)\n\nCasting Time: Reaction, which you take in response to taking damage from a creature that you can see within 60 feet of yourself\nRange: 60 feet\nComponents: V, S\nDuration: Instantaneous\n\nThe creature that damaged you is momentarily surrounded by green flames. It makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 2d10 Fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nUsing a Higher-Level Spell Slot. The damage increases by 1d10 for each spell slot level above 1.",
      "classes": [
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/warlock"
        }
      ],
      "savingThrowAbility": "Dexterity",
      "damage": [
        {
          "damageType": "Fire",
          "damageRoll": {
            "expression": "2d10",
            "count": 2,
            "sides": 10
          }
        }
      ],
      "scalesWithSlotLevel": true,
      "concentration": false,
      "ritual": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/spells/heroes-feast",
      "@type": "Spell",
      "name": "Heroes' Feast",
      "slug": "heroes-feast",
      "source": {
        "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/sources/srd-5-2-1"
      },
      "sourceLocator": {
        "chapter": "Spells",
        "section": "7.196",
        "heading": "Heroes' Feast",
        "lineStart": 9998,
        "lineEnd": 10009
      },
      "level": 6,
      "school": "Conjuration",
      "classAvailability": [
        "Bard",
        "Cleric",
        "Druid"
      ],
      "castingTime": "10 minutes",
      "range": "Self",
      "components": "V, S, M (a gem-encrusted bowl worth 1,000+ GP, which the spell consumes)",
      "duration": "Instantaneous",
      "rulesText": "Level 6 Conjuration (Bard, Cleric, Druid)\n\nCasting Time: 10 minutes\nRange: Self\nComponents: V, S, M (a gem-encrusted bowl worth 1,000+ GP, which the spell consumes)\nDuration: Instantaneous\n\nYou conjure a feast that appears on a surface in an unoccupied 10-foot Cube next to you. The feast takes 1 hour to consume and disappears at the end of that time, and the beneficial effects don't set in until this hour is over. Up to twelve creatures can partake of the feast.\n\nA creature that partakes gains several benefits, which last for 24 hours. The creature has Resistance to Poison damage, and it has Immunity to the Frightened and Poisoned conditions. Its Hit Point maximum also increases by 2d10, and it gains the same number of Hit Points.",
      "classes": [
        {
          "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/classes/bard"
        },
        {
